ss="related-post-item" href="what-is-spooling-in-an-operating-system"><h3 class="h3">What is Spooling in an Operating System</h3><p class="related-post-content">In the operating systems, managing input and output (I/O) devices efficiently is crucial for maintaining high system performance and user productivity. Devices like printers, plotters, and storage media operate at significantly slower speeds compared to the CPU and memory. To bridge this performance gap, operating...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 11 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></svg></span></p></a></li><li><a class="related-post-item" href="what-is-operating-system"><h3 class="h3">What is Operating system</h3><p class="related-post-content">Introduction Operating System (OS) in the field of the modern computer is considered to be the "system software" that primarily serves as a bridge between computer hardware and the user. It is also responsible for the purpose of managing out the hardware resources and also provides...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 8 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3